1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,420
What things make you laugh?
什么事物会让你发笑？

2
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:07,170
There are many things that make us chuckle or burst into laughter.
生活中有很多事情能让我们忍不住轻笑或是捧腹大笑。

3
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:17,470
This natural show of emotion gives off signals that we are happy, we find something humorous or even that we’re just a barrel of laughs!
这种自然的情绪表达会传递出我们很开心、觉得某件事很有趣，甚至我们是开心果的信号！

4
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:23,350
Gelotologists have been looking at why we do it and what the benefits are.
笑学家们一直在研究人类发笑的原因以及笑能带来的益处。

5
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:27,020
Laughter is a very primitive way of making a sound.
笑是一种非常原始的发声方式。

6
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:42,740
When we do it, we make very strange noises – from wheezes and squeaks to gasps and snorts – and each sound simply reflects the muscles in the chest squeezing out air from our ribcages under very high pressure.
当我们笑的时候，会发出各种奇怪的声音——从喘息声、尖细的笑声到倒吸气声、鼻息声都有，每一种声音都源于胸腔肌肉在高压下将空气挤出胸腔的过程。

7
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:50,950
Most of the time our laughter is involuntary and contagious, particularly between friends.
大多数时候，我们的笑是无意识且具有感染力的，在朋友之间尤其如此。

8
00:00:50,950 --> 00:00:56,570
Neuroscientist, Sophie Scott, told the BBC that it’s “a social emotion.
神经科学家索菲·斯科特在接受BBC采访时表示，笑“是一种社交性的情绪。

9
00:00:56,570 --> 00:00:59,340
It’s better to laugh with people we like.”
和自己喜欢的人一起笑，会更愉悦”。

10
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:11,530
She defines two types of laughter – spontaneous laughter, where we laugh instantly and uncontrollably, and conversational laughter – where we laugh together with friends.
她将笑分为两种类型——自发性的笑，也就是那种不由自主、瞬间爆发的笑，以及交谈式的笑，即和朋友们一起时产生的笑声。

11
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:18,530
Research found, on average, people laugh seven times for every ten minutes of conversation.
研究发现，人们平均每十分钟的对话中就会笑七次。

12
00:01:18,530 --> 00:01:24,610
The BBC World Service programme Crowd Science examined the science of laughter.
英国广播公司全球服务节目《大众科学》探究了笑的科学原理。

13
00:01:24,610 --> 00:01:29,440
It wanted to know what caused this highly infectious repetitive action.
该节目试图找出这种极具感染力的重复性行为背后的原因。

14
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:38,810
It found we use laughter to show others that we’re being playful and non-threatening, and this serves to make and maintain social bonds.
研究发现，我们通过笑向他人传递出“我们在开玩笑，没有恶意”的信号，这有助于建立和维系社交关系。

15
00:01:38,810 --> 00:01:48,010
Also, people outside of our social group can understand the relationship between the laughers by the sound of our chuckles.
此外，社交圈子之外的人也能通过笑声的特点，判断出发笑者之间的关系。

16
00:01:48,010 --> 00:02:02,620
While our health is no laughing matter, research has found a good guffaw can help our body and mind – it can make us feel good and relax our bodies. It also helps us manage pain and improve our immune system.
虽然健康问题绝非儿戏，但研究发现，开怀大笑对我们的身心都大有裨益——它能让我们心情愉悦，放松身体，还有助于缓解疼痛、增强免疫系统。

17
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:08,870
That’s why laughter therapy is being used as an alternative to conventional treatments.
这也是为什么笑声疗法正被用作传统疗法的替代方案。

18
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:13,520
But generally, our ability to laugh is out of our control.
不过通常来说，我们发笑的本能是不受控制的。

19
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:18,960
When you start doing it, just go with the flow and others will join in.
当你笑起来的时候，只管顺其自然，身边的人自然会跟着一起笑。
